      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption/permeability records for related beta-blockers show measurable solubility and permeability: labetalol is high-solubility with rat jejunum Peff 2.7e-5 cm/s (C119,C117); sotalol has Caco-2 A-B Papp about 2.9e-6 cm/s (C123,C106); acebutolol has Papp 2.94e-6 cm/s and pH 7 solubility 4.08 mg/mL (C130,C133); atenolol shows intestinal perfusion values in the 0.2-5e-6 cm/s range (C104,C132,C144,C134,C113,C107).",
      "card_ids": ["C119","C117","C123","C106","C130","C133","C104","C132","C144","C134","C113","C107"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall records show that P-gp efflux does not by itself imply F<20: labetalol is a P-gp substrate whose efflux is reduced by verapamil (C162) and has Caco-2 A-B Papp 5.96e-6 cm/s (C153); sotalol is a P-gp substrate with efflux diminished by GG918 (C158,C167) yet L1 records report F approximately 80-100% (C11,C16); atenolol has measurable human jejunal Peff 0.20e-4 cm/s (C151) and no affirmative low-F outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C151","C153","C158","C162","C167","C11","C16"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "PEPT1-mediated absorptive transport is documented for peptide-like drugs (bestatin C161,C165; ceftibuten C197; enalapril C152; temocaprilate C183; 4-aminophenylacetic acid C196). The query's 2-aminothiazole-acetamide motif is structurally reminiscent of these substrates, providing a supportive absorptive mechanism, though no query-specific PEPT1 data exist.",
      "card_ids": ["C161","C165","C197","C152","C183","C196"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low in vitro permeability/efflux markers do not establish F<20: SAHA has low Caco-2 Papp (C188) yet human F is 43% (C23); the only negative mechanistic records (C173 efflux ratio 4.5; C193 ritonavir efflux ratio 142) are for unrelated scaffolds, lack F outcomes, and are not transferable to the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C188","C23","C173","C193"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C151","C152","C153","C158","C161","C162","C165","C167","C177","C183","C188","C196","C197"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific oral bioavailability or IV-comparison data are available.",
    "No query-specific P-gp efflux or intestinal metabolism measurements exist.",
    "PEPT1 applicability to the query is inferred from structural analogy only; the query lacks the free carboxylate typical of many PEPT1 substrates.",
    "L5 records are for reference molecules, so transfer to the query is indirect.",
    "No affirmative low-F comparator context for the query scaffold was available.",
    "Gut-wall CYP3A-type metabolism was not directly measured for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal-metabolism records provide no affirmative low-F evidence; related beta-blockers with P-gp efflux (labetalol, sotalol) have F 36-100%, PEPT1-mediated uptake supports absorption for peptide-like motifs, and low Caco-2/efflux markers (SAHA) coexist with F 43%. The high prediction is strengthened with moderate confidence."
}

